35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears that consumption varies wildly between rooms, with some using four times more than others. Interestingly, fixed rates seem to encourage a more relaxed atmosphere.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, the paperwork is a nightmare! Even with a template, it's so tedious. And seeing another house do it... it takes so much time every month!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,My research confirms that payments are often late and disputes arise whenever the amount changes. The transition when the house filled up was particularly messy.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The bills are incredibly volatile; February is nearly triple August. Furthermore, installing individual meters would be quite expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that some rooms get no sun and need heat much earlier. Also, some people were so worried about the bill they suffered in the heat.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minato, that is a concerning point. If people are afraid to use the utilities they pay for, the house becomes a place of stress rather than a home.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, 34,000 yen per room?! That's way too expensive! We can't spend that much just to figure out who owes what!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the disparity in usage you found explains why some feel they are carrying others. It is not just a rumor; it is a physical reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, the volatility I found makes a simple split difficult. If we just divide by five, the winter spikes will be a heavy burden for everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,I don't like that people were sweating just to save money. It makes the house feel sad.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If we want to avoid the ""coat in February"" scenario, we need a system that removes the fear of the switch. A fixed rate might be the answer.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But @Benjamin, who is going to do the math? If we have to reconcile everything at the end of the year, it'll be a giant mountain of work!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, a bit of work is better than a house full of resentment. We need a system that is transparent so no one feels cheated.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,We must balance the desire for fairness with the actual cost of implementation. Individual meters are likely too costly for our current budget.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,I just want a way where we don't have to send reminders that sound like accusations.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
