60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have three options. A is a flat monthly share, B is a seasonal fixed rate with year-end settlement, and C is per-room metering.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C is out for me! The electrician's quote was huge, and the work to manage it sounds like a total drag.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is the simplest, but it doesn't solve the issue of usage disparity. Option B provides stability but requires a final reckoning.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is risky because of the winter spikes. Option B spreads the cost, but Option C is financially prohibitive for the initial setup.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option B sounds nice because it's more predictable, so we won't be as surprised by the bills.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I strongly favor Option B. It eliminates the psychological barrier to using heat and electricity, making the living environment much more comfortable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, if we do Option B, can we make the year-end settlement simple? I really don't want to spend my whole weekend on a spreadsheet!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, it is a small price to pay for peace. I believe Option B is the most equitable way to handle the seasonal shifts without constant arguing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"While Option A is the cheapest to start, Option B is more rational for budgeting. It prevents the ""second rent"" feeling in winter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,I agree with everyone! Option B seems like the kindest way to do it.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a consensus. Option B provides the psychological comfort I value and the stability Victoria seeks.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"If everyone else is okay with it, I'm in! As long as we don't make the year-end part too scary.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for Option B. It addresses the volatility and the resentment by creating a predictable baseline.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option B is the most sustainable choice that avoids the high cost of meters while managing the winter peaks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option B too! Let's just be happy and cozy.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
